| Block | Friendly label | C++ form | Help | Fields | Inputs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| \`functions.make\` (definition) | \`define %NAME with … returns %RETURNS\` | \`%RETURNS %NAME(…)\` | Help for functions.make. | \`NAME\`: the name of the new function. \`RETURNS\`: a type, \`void\`, \`int\` or \`std::string\`, default \`void\`. | \`BODY\`: blocks. Setting \`params\`: up to 16 parameters, each \`int\`. |
| \`functions.use\` (reporter, gives the type of \`FUNC\`) | \`%FUNC %ARG …\` | \`%FUNC(%ARG, …)\` | Help for functions.use. | \`FUNC\`: the function it uses. | \`ARG0\`, \`ARG1\`, …: any value, one for each of \`argCount\`; required. Setting \`argCount\`: 0 to 16, default 0. |

## In the toolbox

1. \`functions.make\`

*My Blocks*: the editor also adds a call block for every function of the project: \`functions.use\`.
